\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord and Saviour, true and kind,
\par Be the master of my mind;
\par Bless and guide and strengthen still
\par All my powers of thought and will.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. While I ply the scholar's task,
\par Jesus Christ, be near, I ask;
\par Help the memory, clear the brain,
\par Knowledge still to seek and gain.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Here I train for life's swift race;
\par Let me do it in Thy grace:
\par Here I arm me for life's fight;
\par Let me do it in Thy might.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thou hast made me mind and soul;
\par I for Thee would use the whole:
\par Thou hast died that I might live;
\par All my powers to Thee I give.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Striving, thinking, learning still,
\par Let me follow thus Thy will,
\par Till my whole glad nature be
\par Trained for duty and for Thee.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

